.         * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
. 
.         * Model description: Linear regression regressing political partisans
> hip on having a daughter rather 
.         * than a son as first child with some sociodemographic controls. The 
> idea is that having a daughter 
.         * as a first child is randomly distributed among parents and uncorrel
> ated with unobserved characteristics
.         * of parents. Excluding multiple births and estimating robust cluster
> ed standard errors at the household level.
. 
. 
.         reg left i.daughter c.age i.edu i.fam i.gender i.west i.work i.syear,
>  vce(cluster hid)          

